{title: 577 - In the Heart of Jesus}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #577 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 577}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]In the [G]heart of [Csus7]Je [C7]sus
[F]There is [Bb]love for [F]you,
[F]Love most [G7]pure and [C]tender,
[Dm]Love most [G7]deep and [C]tr[C7]ue;
[F]Why should [F7]you be [Bbsus]lone[Bb]ly,
[D7]Why for friendship [Gm]sigh,
When the [F]heart [C7]of [F]Jesus
[G]Has a [C7]full [F]supply?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]In the [G]mind of Jesus [Csus7]there is [C7]thought for you,
[F]Warm as [Bb]summer sunshine, sweet [F]as morning dew;
[F]Why should you [G7]be fearful, why [C]take anxious thought,
[Dm]Since the [G7]mind of Jesus [C]cares for [C7]those He bought?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]In the [G]field of Jesus [Csus7]there is [C7]work for you;
[F]Such as [Bb]even angels might [F]rejoice to do;
[F]Why stand [G7]idly sighing for [C]some lifework grand,
[Dm]While the [G7]field of [C]Jesus seeks [C7]your reaping hand?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]In the [G]home of Jesus [Csus7]there's a [C7]place for you;
[F]Glorious, bright, [Bb]and joyous, calm [F]and peaceful too;
[F]Why then, like [G7]a wanderer, roam [C]with weary pace,
[Dm]If the [G7]home of Jesus [C]holds for [C7]you a place?
{end_of_verse}
